   $q$Read the sentence: "Lena walked slowly and tiredly up the steep hill." Which revision uses one precise verb in place of "walked slowly and tiredly"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Lena trudged up the steep hill.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Lena went up the steep hill.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-verb"},{"text":"Lena dashed up the steep hill.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-connotation"},{"text":"Lena skipped up the steep hill.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-connotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Lena trudged up the steep hill.$q$, $q$"Trudged" means walked slowly and heavily, as when tired, so it captures the whole idea. "Skipped" and "dashed" are precise verbs, but they suggest energy and speed.$q$, 'draft', null)
