   $q$Read the sentence: "The coach told us to stretch carefully, drink water, and that we should rest on Sunday." Which revision fixes the faulty parallel structure?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The coach told us to stretch carefully, drinking water, and rest on Sunday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mixed-verb-forms"},{"text":"The coach told us stretching carefully, drink water, and that we should rest on Sunday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-in-series"},{"text":"The coach told us to stretch carefully, to drink water, and that we should rest on Sunday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"partial-parallel-fix"},{"text":"The coach told us to stretch carefully, drink water, and rest on Sunday.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The coach told us to stretch carefully, drink water, and rest on Sunday.$q$, $q$"Stretch," "drink," and "rest" are all base verbs that follow "to," so the list is parallel. Adding a second "to" does not help while the last item is still the clause "that we should rest."$q$, 'draft', null)
