  ('7b6272a2-239b-5af4-9215-55bad981a544', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-sentence-structure'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence about the bridge is correct as written?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The bridge had stood for nearly a century however engineers who inspected it last spring found cracks in two supports, so the city closed it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conjunctive-adverb-fused"},{"text":"The bridge had stood for nearly a century, engineers who inspected it last spring found cracks in two supports, so the city closed it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"},{"text":"Although the bridge had stood for nearly a century, engineers who inspected it last spring found cracks in two supports, so the city closed it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Although the bridge had stood for nearly a century and engineers who inspected it last spring found cracks in two supports.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"long-dependent-clause-as-sentence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Although the bridge had stood for nearly a century, engineers who inspected it last spring found cracks in two supports, so the city closed it.$q$, $q$The sentence opens with a dependent "Although" clause, then joins two independent clauses with ", so," which is correct even though the sentence is long. The choice that begins "Although the bridge had stood for nearly a century and engineers" is only a long "Although" clause with no main clause, so it is a fragment.$q$, 'draft', null)
