   $q$Which group of words is a sentence fragment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Built long ago, the lighthouse still stands on the rocky point.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introductory-participle-read-as-fragment"},{"text":"That the lighthouse still stands surprises many visitors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"noun-clause-subject-read-as-fragment"},{"text":"The old lighthouse on the rocky point, which sailors relied on for over a hundred years before the modern beacon was installed.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Listen closely to the foghorn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"imperative-read-as-fragment"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The old lighthouse on the rocky point, which sailors relied on for over a hundred years before the modern beacon was installed.$q$, $q$"The old lighthouse" is never given a main verb; "relied" and "was installed" belong to the "which" and "before" clauses. "That the lighthouse still stands surprises many visitors" is complete because the noun clause is the subject of "surprises."$q$, 'draft', null)
