   $q$The writer wants sentence 4 to support the claim more clearly. Which revision does that best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ibarra also notes that the keeper's old logbook can be seen today in a small town museum.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-claim-detail"},{"text":"Ibarra also notes that the keeper recorded the weather in a logbook every single day of the year, holidays included.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Ibarra also notes that the keeper's logbook was bound in thick brown leather with a brass clasp.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Ibarra also notes, in a very interesting part of the article, that the keeper wrote in a logbook.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ibarra also notes that the keeper recorded the weather in a logbook every single day of the year, holidays included.$q$, $q$Adding that the record was kept every day, holidays included, shows why the job was demanding, which is the claim in sentence 2. Calling the detail "very interesting" adds no evidence at all.$q$, 'draft', 'ea7b79be-9e7f-58c6-9d9f-a5b7458c66e9')
