-- Passage wg8-writing-with-evidence-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('362be4b9-3af6-5c86-8e57-b3f540a62e51', 'wg8-writing-with-evidence-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: The Bees That Live Alone$q$, $q$(1) In "The Bees That Live Alone," Sung-min Park explains that most bee species do not live in hives. (2) ____. (3) Park writes that "about nine out of ten bee species live alone," nesting in small holes in wood or soil. (4) Because they have no hive to guard, these bees rarely sting. (5) Park also explains that one mason bee can pollinate as many flowers as dozens of honeybees. (6) This is because the mason bee carries pollen loosely on its belly, so it drops more pollen on each flower.

(7) Park ends by describing a class that built a "bee hotel" from hollow plant stems. (8) Within a month, the students counted thirty sealed nesting tubes. (9) Honey is a sweet food that people have eaten for thousands of years. (10) This result shows that ordinary people can help solitary bees with simple projects.

(11) ____$q$, 'draft')
