values ('f10969c8-3da3-54c7-a142-f56f2f62264c', 'wg8-writing-with-evidence-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: The Rolling Classroom$q$, $q$(1) In "The Rolling Classroom," Ezekiel Moana describes a school bus that was rebuilt into a science lab for rural students in Pine Hollow County. (2) Moana suggests that the lab gave students experiences their own schools could not offer. (3) He explains that the county's three small schools shared one microscope among them. (4) The bus, by contrast, carried twelve microscopes, a weather station and a small telescope. (5) Moana quotes science teacher Adaeze Nwosu, who said students "lined up before sunrise when the bus came to town." (6) ____.

(7) The lab also changed what students hoped to do later. (8) Moana reports that after two years, twice as many Pine Hollow students signed up for advanced science classes in high school. (9) The bus is painted bright yellow with green stripes. (10) One student, Lupe Ortega, told Moana she now plans to study weather.

(11) Moana's article shows that bringing science to students can open doors that distance once closed.$q$, 'draft')
