   $q$Which revision of sentence (3) best states a clear claim for the essay?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The town council should restore the Kessler Park bandstand instead of replacing it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bandstand is very, very old and has been standing for a long time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fact-not-claim"},{"text":"Kessler Park has many trees, benches and paths that visitors enjoy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"},{"text":"Some people like the bandstand, and some people do not like it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-position"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The town council should restore the Kessler Park bandstand instead of replacing it.$q$, $q$A claim takes a position that the rest of the essay supports, and the draft argues for restoring the bandstand. Repeating that the bandstand is old states a fact, not a position.$q$, 'draft', 'b643b1e3-f9c4-5906-84b2-ce90f12f9dca')
