   $q$The writer wants to revise sentence 3 so that it introduces the main idea of the whole report. Which revision does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Instead, they are taking part in one of the many activities that nature centers offer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"Instead, they are taking part in bird banding, which is the most enjoyable job at the center.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-focus"},{"text":"Instead, they are taking part in bird banding, a method that lets scientists follow individual birds to learn where they travel and how their numbers change.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Instead, they are taking part in bird banding, which shows where warblers fly each winter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Instead, they are taking part in bird banding, a method that lets scientists follow individual birds to learn where they travel and how their numbers change.$q$, $q$The correct revision defines bird banding and previews both main ideas: travel routes (paragraph 3) and changing numbers (paragraph 4). The warbler version is too narrow because it covers only one example from paragraph 3.$q$, 'draft', 'b29335a3-ddab-5b88-a2d0-592a0d4d7f96')
