  ('5a056c4e-0c0a-5aca-9aab-079680d17893', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-informative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A reader asks why it matters that a swept stone "curves less." Which sentence, added after sentence 9, best answers this question?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The pebble is created by sprinkling drops of water before each game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-detail"},{"text":"This means sweepers can help a stone that was released slightly off line travel straight enough to reach the house.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Some sweepers wear special shoes with soles that grip the ice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Stones that curve less are usually thrown by the most experienced players.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$This means sweepers can help a stone that was released slightly off line travel straight enough to reach the house.$q$, $q$The correct sentence explains the practical effect of less curve: it can keep a stone on target. The sentence about experienced players makes a claim the report never supports and does not explain why reduced curve matters.$q$, 'draft', 'cbbbbbcc-5e85-59e4-8c34-7d2987c29364')
