values ('8b573f7a-948f-51d3-82a9-ccc95aa69704', 'wg9-informative-writing-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-informative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Salt Marshes as Storm Barriers$q$, $q$(1) Along the coast of Marlow County, wide meadows of grass grow in shallow water where rivers meet the sea. (2) These areas are called salt marshes. (3) They are wetlands that flood with salt water at high tide and drain at low tide.

(4) Salt marshes protect nearby towns during storms. (5) The dense grasses slow down incoming waves, and the spongy soil absorbs extra water like a giant towel. (6) A study by the Marlow Coastal Research Center found that waves lost about half their height after crossing 40 meters of marsh. (7) Towns behind wide marshes reported less flood damage after Storm Delia in 2018 than towns without them.

(8) Marshes are also nurseries for wildlife. (9) Young fish and crabs hide among the grass stems, where larger predators have trouble reaching them. (10) Seagulls are my favorite birds to watch when I visit the beach.

(11) Unfortunately, Marlow County has lost about a third of its salt marshes since 1950. (12) Many were filled in with soil to build houses, roads and parking lots. (13) Now the county is trying to restore them. (14) Volunteers have planted more than 60,000 grass seedlings along the shore since 2020.$q$, 'draft')
