insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('0ec56326-5c85-568e-a839-5e4ef83fbb48', 'wg9-narrative-writing-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Three Steps on an Index Card$q$, $q$(1) My grandmother, whom everyone calls Lola, had owned a tablet for a year and used it only as a very expensive clock. (2) In May, my cousin Marisol was graduating from college in another state, and Lola could not make the long trip. (3) The ceremony would be shown online, and the family decided I would be the one to teach Lola how to watch it and call in afterward.

(4) Our first lesson did not go well. (5) Lola tapped the screen so hard that she opened four apps at once. (6) "This machine does not like me," she said, frowning at it. (7) I tried to explain everything at once: the camera, the microphone, the volume, and the link. (8) By the end of the afternoon, we were both tired, and she had not made a single call.

(9) The next Sunday, I tried a different plan. (10) I wrote three steps on an index card in large letters and taped it to the kitchen table. (11) We practiced only the first step until she could do it without looking at the card. (12) Then we added the second step, and later the third. (13) On the fourth Sunday, she called me from her bedroom while I sat in the kitchen, and her laughing face filled my screen.

(14) On graduation day, Lola watched the whole ceremony, and when Marisol crossed the stage, she waved at the tablet as if Marisol could see her. (15) The tablet's battery lasts for about ten hours on a full charge.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
