   $q$Read the sentences: "The art teacher brought in unusual materials. Such as cardboard tubes, bottle caps, and old maps." Which revision fixes the fragment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The art teacher brought in unusual materials, such as cardboard tubes, bottle caps, and old maps.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The art teacher brought in unusual materials. Such as cardboard tubes, bottle caps, and old maps, for example.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-unfixed"},{"text":"The art teacher brought in unusual materials; such as cardboard tubes, bottle caps, and old maps.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-phrase"},{"text":"The art teacher brought in unusual materials, they were cardboard tubes, bottle caps, and old maps.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The art teacher brought in unusual materials, such as cardboard tubes, bottle caps, and old maps.$q$, $q$"Such as cardboard tubes, bottle caps, and old maps" is a phrase that lists examples, so it attaches to the sentence with a comma. A semicolon cannot come before a phrase that lacks its own subject and verb.$q$, 'draft', null)
