   $q$Read the sentence: "The town replaced its streetlights with LED bulbs, this change cut the electric bill nearly in half." Which revision fixes the error?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The town replaced its streetlights with LED bulbs, a change that cut the electric bill nearly in half.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The town replaced its streetlights with LED bulbs, this change cut the electric bill nearly in half.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"pronoun-this-splice"},{"text":"The town replaced its streetlights with LED bulbs this change cut the electric bill nearly in half.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"The town replaced its streetlights with LED bulbs, as a result, the change cut the electric bill nearly in half.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conjunctive-adverb-with-comma-only"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The town replaced its streetlights with LED bulbs, a change that cut the electric bill nearly in half.$q$, $q$"A change that cut the electric bill" is a phrase that renames the first clause's action, so a comma before it is correct. Starting the second part with "this change" makes it an independent clause, so the original is a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
