   $q$The draft never states its main claim. Which sentence, added after sentence 1, would best state a claim the evidence supports?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Brandt's study proves that still stretches are dangerous and should be banned in every sport.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstatement"},{"text":"Many soccer teams warm up before games, and some teams warm up longer than others do.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Warming up is boring, so young players should be allowed to skip it before practice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-opinion"},{"text":"Brandt's findings show that moving warm-ups prepare players' bodies for soccer better than still stretches do.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Brandt's findings show that moving warm-ups prepare players' bodies for soccer better than still stretches do.$q$, $q$The draft compares two warm-ups and shows the moving one led to faster sprints and fewer missed practices, so the claim should say that. The choice about banning stretches in every sport claims far more than a study of sixty soccer players can prove.$q$, 'draft', 'bd5f01da-1909-5142-a91a-1d328e26d8ef')
