insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('4e31bf17-6d41-5668-8cfc-b8508b36c22c', 'wg9-writing-with-evidence-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Learning to Share the Spotlight$q$, $q$(1) In Nadia Ferreira's short story "Second Chair," a trumpet player named Mateo learns that being a good musician means more than being the best one in the room. (2) At the start of the story, Mateo has played first chair in his school band for two years. (3) When a new student named Priya wins the first chair audition, Mateo "stared at the list until the letters blurred." (4) ____ (5) For the next week, he refuses to look at Priya during rehearsals and practices his solo loudly in the hallway so that everyone can hear.

(6) Mateo begins to change when the band prepares for the spring concert. (7) During one rehearsal, Priya misses her entrance in a difficult passage, and the whole band stops. (8) Instead of smiling, Mateo quietly plays the first two notes of her part so she can find her place. (9) Later, he stays after school to help her practice the hardest measures. (10) The story is set in a small town that hosts a music festival every summer. (11) By the end, Mateo stands beside Priya at the concert, and Ferreira writes that "the two trumpets sounded like one."

(12) ____$q$, 'draft')
