   $q$Which statement best explains why sentence 5 strengthens the writer's analysis?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that Mateo is a better trumpet player than Priya and should have won the audition.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It explains the rules for how first chair auditions work in most school bands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It gives specific actions that show Mateo's jealousy, which sets up a clear contrast with his later kindness.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the story's main conflict is between Mateo and the band director.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-conflict"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It gives specific actions that show Mateo's jealousy, which sets up a clear contrast with his later kindness.$q$, $q$A character's change is easiest to see when the draft shows both the before and the after, and sentence 5 gives the before. Nothing in the draft suggests Mateo is the better player, so that choice is an unsupported inference.$q$, 'draft', '4e31bf17-6d41-5668-8cfc-b8508b36c22c')
