-- Passage wg9-writing-with-evidence-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('0f289b91-dfa0-52ae-ad8d-faf331dc736f', 'wg9-writing-with-evidence-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Letters Across the Years$q$, $q$(1) Journalist Hana Lindqvist's article "Dear Friend" describes a program at Ridgeview High School that pairs forty ninth graders with residents of a nearby senior center as pen pals. (2) Lindqvist's reporting shows that the letters benefit both generations, not just the older adults. (3) Each student writes one handwritten letter a month and receives a reply within about two weeks. (4) According to the center's activities director, residents who join the program are more likely to attend group events and to talk about their pen pals with staff. (5) ____ (6) Lindqvist also quotes a ninth grader who says that writing letters "made me slow down and actually think about what I wanted to say."

(7) Some readers might argue that letters are old-fashioned when video calls are so easy. (8) ____ (9) Lindqvist notes that several residents have trouble hearing on calls but can reread a letter as many times as they like. (10) Handwriting also takes time, which shows the reader that the writer cared enough to make the effort. (11) Ridgeview High School was built in 1962 and has a large football stadium.

(12) Overall, Lindqvist's article shows that a simple letter can build real friendships across generations.$q$, 'draft')
