  ('d71bf237-0585-5ade-874c-49186b686d23', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer wants to add one more piece of evidence from Tanaka's article to support the claim in sentence 2. Which detail would be most relevant?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Tanaka himself began drawing as a child at his grandmother's kitchen table.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-anecdote"},{"text":"A few visitors said the museum's pencils were too short and hard to hold.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-point-detail"},{"text":"The museum gave away more than three thousand sketchbooks during the first year of the program.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"popularity-not-evidence"},{"text":"When shown a photo of the painting later, sketchers could point out about nine details, and non-sketchers about two.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$When shown a photo of the painting later, sketchers could point out about nine details, and non-sketchers about two.$q$, $q$Sentence 2 claims sketchers notice far more, and a direct count of details remembered measures exactly that. The number of sketchbooks given away shows the program was popular, not that it helped people notice more.$q$, 'draft', '1e122d82-b647-57bc-8510-ed2ddb338831')
