   $q$Which sentence would best fill the blank in sentence 4 by giving evidence that the table cuts food waste?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Haddad reports that in two months, students left more than 1,500 items on the table, and nearly all were taken.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Haddad thinks that the share table is a very clever and creative idea.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-evidence"},{"text":"The cafeteria at Westbrook High School has long tables and seats about three hundred students.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Yogurt is a good source of protein, and apples are a good source of fiber.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Haddad reports that in two months, students left more than 1,500 items on the table, and nearly all were taken.$q$, $q$Fifteen hundred items taken by other students instead of thrown away is direct evidence of less waste. Haddad's opinion that the idea is clever does not show any food was actually saved.$q$, 'draft', '602f6ab6-9b85-57fe-8cfa-73635c90d39c')
